     1	# the external party Inference Lab — gated benchmark access
     2	
     3	Built 2026-08-25. Temporary, gated access for the external party (https://the external party.ai / llm.the external party.ai) to
     4	benchmark the RTX Pro 6000 and the GB10. No production machine is directly reachable.
     5	
     6	## Architecture
     7	
     8	```
     9	the external party → the bench hostname  (CF Access, allowed-email policy, session 24h)
    10	     → cloudflared tunnel "the external party-bench-bastion" (4b1cfef2-549e-499e-8a07-fa6027db78fd)
    11	     → CT 204 the external party-bastion (node2, <lan-address> + <island-address> on island)
    12	        ├→ CT 205 the external party-bench-rtx  <island-address>:22  (isolated SDN vnet cirub0)
    13	        └→ GB10 the external party-bench container  <lan-address>   [NOT YET BUILT]
    14	```
    15	
    16	- **CF side** (account 3e3fc5cb…, zone <estate-domain>): tunnel `the external party-bench-bastion`,
    17	  CNAME `ssh-bench` → tunnel, Access app `the external party bench SSH` (493b20ef…), policy
    18	  `the external party-bench-allowed-emails` (43af5936…) — currently <email> only.
    19	- **CT 204 the external party-bastion** (1c/1G/8G, vmbr0 .204 + cirub0 <island-address>, onboot=1):
    20	  cloudflared connector; sshd key-only, user `the external party` (NO sudo); nftables drops all
    21	  private-range egress except <island-address>:22 and <lan-address>; tinyproxy
    22	  :8888 + dnsmasq :53 serve the island (only <island-address> allowed).
    23	- **CT 205 the external party-bench-rtx** (12c/32G/120G local-lvm, onboot=0, unprivileged):
    24	  on SDN vnet `cirub0` (zone `cirub`, node2-only, NO uplink — physical L2 island,
    25	  no NAT anywhere). GPU via /dev/nvidia* bind mounts + cgroup allows c 195/510
    26	  (same pattern as CT 201). NVIDIA user-space 610.43.02 via .run --no-kernel-modules
    27	  (matches node2 host driver EXACTLY — if node2 driver is upgraded, rerun the .run
    28	  in 205 with the new version). User `the external party` HAS passwordless sudo (his sandbox).
    29	  Internet only via bastion tinyproxy (http/https, set in /etc/profile.d/proxy.sh,
    30	  apt.conf.d/95proxy). Verified: HF reachable, Infisical/PBS NOT reachable.
    31	  Excluded from the hourly PBS job (exclude=114,205) — scratch box, 120G churn.
    32	- **GB10**: NOT built (permission classifier blocked remote execution on gb10; the owner
    33	  runs it). Staged script: `<path> external party-bench/gb10_setup.sh` — runs as `<login-user>`
    34	  (docker group, no sudo needed): `scp <path> external party-bench/gb10_setup.sh gb10:~ && ssh gb10 bash gb10_setup.sh`.
    35	  Design: docker-native only (no host iptables/systemd): bench container on an
    36	  `--internal` network (no outbound), socat relay container publishes .225:2222→bench:22,
    37	  squid proxy container (172.30.99.3:3128) allows internet but denies RFC1918.
    38	  All state under `/home/<login-user>/the external party-bench/` on gb10.
    39	
    40	## Onboarding the external party (when email + SSH pubkey arrive)
    41	
    42	1. Add his email to the Access policy (script `cf_add_email.py` pattern, or dash:
    43	   Zero Trust → Access → Applications → "the external party bench SSH" → policy → add email).
    44	2. Append his pubkey to `/home/the external party/.ssh/authorized_keys` in CT 204 AND CT 205
    45	   (`pct exec` from node2), and in the GB10 container home once built
    46	   (`/home/<login-user>/the external party-bench/home/.ssh/authorized_keys` on gb10).
    47	3. Send him the client config (needs `cloudflared` installed locally):
    48	
    49	```
    50	Host ssh-bench
    51	  HostName the bench hostname
    52	  User the external party
    53	  ProxyCommand cloudflared access ssh --hostname %h
    54	Host bench-rtx
    55	  HostName <island-address>
    56	  User the external party
    57	  ProxyJump ssh-bench
    58	Host bench-gb10
    59	  HostName <lan-address>
    60	  Port 2222
    61	  User the external party
    62	  ProxyJump ssh-bench
    63	```
    64	
    65	## Benchmark windows (GPU exclusivity)
    66	
    67	- **RTX window open:** `pct exec 201 -- systemctl stop vllm` on node2 (HAL chat
    68	  fails over down limp-router rungs; expect degraded latency, not outage).
    69	  Verify VRAM free: `pct exec 205 -- nvidia-smi`. **Close:** start vllm back,
    70	  verify LiteLLM route healthy. Check cluster tasks before touching anything
    71	  (avoid :00 vzdump windows).
    72	- **GB10 window open:** `docker stop vllm-qwen3-30b vllm-rerank vllm-embed` and
    73	  `docker update --memory 100g the external party-bench`. Note: GB10 Qwen3 seat is the tribunal
    74	  backstop — don't open a window while a panel run is in flight. **Close:**
    75	  `docker update --memory 20g the external party-bench`, start the three vLLM containers.
    76	- Coordinate against hale-brain teacher/distillation runs on GB10.
    77	
    78	## Teardown (end of engagement)
    79	
    80	1. CF: delete Access app 493b20ef… (+policy), DNS CNAME `ssh-bench`, tunnel 4b1cfef2….
    81	2. node2: `pct stop 204 205 && pct destroy 204 205`; remove SDN vnet `cirub0` +
    82	   zone `cirub` (`pvesh delete /cluster/sdn/vnets/cirub0`, `.../zones/cirub`,
    83	   then `pvesh set /cluster/sdn`).
    84	3. GB10: `docker rm -f the external party-bench the external party-proxy the external party-ssh-relay`,
    85	   `docker network rm cirubench`, `rm -rf /home/<login-user>/the external party-bench`, `docker rmi the external party-bench:1`.
    86	4. Backup job: restore exclude to `114` only.
    87	5. If anything of ours was ever typed into his environment (it shouldn't be): rotate.
    88	
    89	## Security posture summary
    90	
    91	- No inbound WAN exposure anywhere (tunnel is outbound-only from CT 204).
    92	- Identity gate at CF edge (email allowlist) BEFORE any packet reaches sshd.
    93	- Bastion user has no root; egress firewall + proxy policy live where he can't touch them.
    94	- CT 205 is on a no-uplink L2 island: LAN unreachable by construction, not by rule.
    95	- CT 205 is unprivileged; GPU shared with CT 201 — isolation is fs/process-level,
    96	  not GPU-level (a driver-crashing workload would still hit vLLM).
    97	- GB10 bench container (once built): internal network, egress only via squid ACL.

